cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Identity — E47 formal layer and the Kouns–Killion Paradigm (KKP-R)"
message: "If you use this formal layer or cite the E47 bridge certificate, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kouns
    given-names: Nicholas Shane
    name-suffix: DO
    affiliation: "AIMS Research Institute, Las Vegas, Nevada"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nicholaskouns-create/Identity"
url: "https://nicholaskouns-create.github.io/e47-formal-validation.html"
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked formal layer for the E47 spectral kernel and the
  Kouns–Killion Paradigm (KKP-R), with paired Lean 4 and Coq developments,
  an axiom-ledger gate, and independent exact-arithmetic validators.
  Certificate E47-BRIDGE-001…011 establishes that E47, the Sigillum wheel and
  the Lifshitz dimensional flow are instances of one functional,
  Omega(A,q) = dim ker q(A) / dim V, and links the renormalisation-group fixed
  point D* = 10 to the degree of the retention polynomial by a degree lock
  proved over the reals. The concrete 125x125 tensor-product matrix is not
  constructed in that certificate; the isotypic model is, and the bridge
  between them remains open.
keywords:
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
  - Coq
  - axiom ledger
  - Casimir operator
  - spectral kernel
  - representation theory
  - commutant
  - anisotropic scaling
  - spectral dimension
  - renormalisation group
  - E47
  - KKP-R
